</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experimental Setup</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We employ GPT-4o <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> as the backbone router and fusion operator within Q-Router. The router is responsible for analyzing the input video descriptors and selecting appropriate expert models, while the fusion operator integrates their outputs into a unified quality report and produces the final quality score on a <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,100]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0,100</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,100]</annotation></semantics></math> scale. For reproducibility, the complete prompts used to deploy GPT-4o, including routing instructions and fusion templates, are provided in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Prompts used in the Routing Process ‣ Q-Router: Agentic Video Quality Assessment with Expert Model Routing and Artifact Localization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As for the routing pool, we include all the baseline models evaluated in this section, which collectively serve as the candidate experts. For UGC VQA, we leverage the publicly released model weights to ensure faithful implementation and evaluation. Since T2VQA does not provide open-sourced model weights, we reproduce its training process by following the official repository<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              https://github.com/QMME/T2VQA</span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Baselines ‣ 3.1 Video Quality Assessment ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Q-Router: Agentic Video Quality Assessment with Expert Model Routing and Artifact Localization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> summarizes the performance of Q-Router compared with state-of-the-art baselines on both UGC and AIGC VQA benchmarks. Our method achieves the best average performance across datasets, with a PLCC of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8539" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.8539</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8539</annotation></semantics></math> and SRCC of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext=".8407" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>.8407</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">.8407</annotation></semantics></math>, outperforming all individual baselines by a significant margin over <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20\%</annotation></semantics></math>, highlighting the effectiveness of the routing-and-fusion paradigm in leveraging complementary strengths of heterogeneous expert models.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On UGC datasets, Q-Router consistently demonstrates superior or highly competitive results. For example, it achieves the best PLCC (<math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8076" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.8076</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8076</annotation></semantics></math>) on LSVQ-1080 and the second-best SRCC (<math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8607" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.8607</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8607</annotation></semantics></math>) on KoNViD-1k, surpassing strong baselines such as COVER <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>, DOVER <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>, and MaxVQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>. Importantly, Q-Router maintains robustness across different datasets, whereas individual baselines often exhibit dataset-specific strengths but lack generalization.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">On the T2VQA-DB dataset, Q-Router significantly outperforms all baselines, reaching a PLCC of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8283" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.8283</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8283</annotation></semantics></math> and SRCC of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8258" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.8258</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8258</annotation></semantics></math>. This demonstrates the Q-Router’s ability to adaptively leverage expert knowledge and handle distribution shifts in AI-generated video quality—a setting where conventional UGC-trained models fail (PLCC <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;0.25</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Visual Question Answering on Video Quality</h3>

<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Datasets</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further conduct experiments on visual question answering tasks related to video quality. Specifically, we evaluate a wide range of VLMs, along with Q-Router, on Q-Bench-Video <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>, which is the first and currently only benchmark dedicated to this task.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Baselines</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We deploy Q-Router with GPT-4o <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> as the backbone, and evaluate it alongside several widely used open-sourced VLMs, including LLaVA-Next <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>, LLaVA-v1.5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>, mPLUG-Owl2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>, mPLUG-Owl3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>, LLaVA-OneVision <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>, InternVL-Chat <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>, VILA1.5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>, PLLaVA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, LLaVA-Next-Video <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>, ST-LLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>, Video-LLaVA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite>, VideoChat2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>, and GPT-4o <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>. These models represent the current generation of multimodal models designed for video understanding and serve as competitive baselines. In addition, we include GPT-4o itself as a strong proprietary baseline, as it currently ranks as the state-of-the-art model on the Q-Bench-Video leaderboard <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experimental Setup</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt the same experimental settings as described in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Video Quality Assessment ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Q-Router: Agentic Video Quality Assessment with Expert Model Routing and Artifact Localization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> for video quality rating, ensuring consistency across evaluation protocols. Specifically, we employ GPT-4o <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> as the backbone router and fusion operator within Q-Router, and construct the routing pool using the same set of expert models introduced earlier. The evaluation is conducted on Q-Bench-Video <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>, a large-scale benchmark designed for video quality question answering, which covers diverse question types (e.g., Yes-or-No, What/How), video modalities (UGC, AIGC, and CG), and contextual reasoning settings (e.g., Referring, Global, and Comparison). To ensure reproducibility, we follow the official evaluation protocol of Q-Bench-Video and report accuracy across all categories as well as the overall score.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:167.6pt;vertical-align:-82.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-56.9pt,27.6pt) scale(0.751914995592585,0.751914995592585) ;">
<table id="S3.T2.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S3.T2.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S3.T2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Method</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S3.T2.3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Overall</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;" colspan="3"><span id="S3.T2.3.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Question type</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;" colspan="4"><span id="S3.T2.3.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Quality Concern</span></td></tr>
