          <span id="alg4.l21.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><math id="alg4.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{sev}\leftarrow\textsc{Pool}(\hat{H};M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">sev</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathsize="0.900em">Pool</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{sev}\leftarrow\textsc{Pool}(\hat{H};M)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg4.l21.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg4.l21.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;float:right;"><math id="alg4.l21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Mean Pooling
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg4.l22.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span id="alg4.l22.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">if</span><span id="alg4.l22.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg4.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{sev}&gt;\text{best}(c).\text{sev}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">sev</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em">&gt;</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">best</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mtext mathsize="0.900em">sev</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{sev}&gt;\text{best}(c).\text{sev}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg4.l22.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg4.l22.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">then</span><span id="alg4.l22.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg4.l23.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">      </span><math id="alg4.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Overlay}\leftarrow\textsc{Blend}(F_{1},\textsc{ColorMap}(\hat{H}),\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝖮𝗏𝖾𝗋𝗅𝖺𝗒</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathsize="0.900em">Blend</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathsize="0.900em">ColorMap</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Overlay}\leftarrow\textsc{Blend}(F_{1},\textsc{ColorMap}(\hat{H}),\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg4.l23.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg4.l24.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">      </span><math id="alg4.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{paths}\leftarrow\textsc{Save}\left(\hat{H},\mathsf{Overlay}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">paths</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathsize="0.900em">Save</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝖮𝗏𝖾𝗋𝗅𝖺𝗒</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{paths}\leftarrow\textsc{Save}\left(\hat{H},\mathsf{Overlay}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg4.l24.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">25:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg4.l25.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">      </span><math id="alg4.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{best}(c)\leftarrow\langle\text{sev},\text{pair}=(t,t\!+\!1),\text{paths}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">best</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">sev</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">pair</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo lspace="0.072em" mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mtext mathsize="0.900em">paths</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{best}(c)\leftarrow\langle\text{sev},\text{pair}=(t,t\!+\!1),\text{paths}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg4.l25.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
     </span>
</div>
<div id="alg4.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg4.l26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">26:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg4.l26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">return</span><span id="alg4.l26.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg4.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\text{best}(c),\text{paths}(c)\}_{c\in\mathcal{C}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">best</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">paths</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒞</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\text{best}(c),\text{paths}(c)\}_{c\in\mathcal{C}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg4.l26.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The artifact localization pipeline (Algorithm <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ Appendix B Details on Artifact Localization ‣ Q-Router: Agentic Video Quality Assessment with Expert Model Routing and Artifact Localization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) integrates probabilistic sampling, VLM-based filtering, perceptual difference analysis, and structured visualization to identify artifact-prone regions in video content. It proceeds in three main stages:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Probabilistic Frame Extraction.</span>
Each video <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> is first processed by the Probabilistic Extractor <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{PE}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖤</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{PE}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, which assigns frame-wise artifact probabilities based on handcrafted features and logistic weighting.
High-probability frames are grouped into clips using the HysteresisClips algorithm with thresholds <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{high}},\tau_{\text{low}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>high</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>low</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{high}},\tau_{\text{low}}</annotation></semantics></math>, enforcing temporal stability and contextual padding <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>.
To ensure coverage, the DiversifiedSelection algorithm further selects frames by combining top-<math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> high-probability samples, farthest-point sampling in HSV space for visual diversity, and mandatory inclusion of shot-boundary frames.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VLM-based Artifact Filtering.</span>
Candidate frames are filtered by a vision–language model <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{VLM}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖵𝖫𝖬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{VLM}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> under a structured prompt that classifies frames into three artifact categories: (1) visual hallucinations, (2) image artifacts, or (3) AI-generated inconsistencies.
Only frames flagged with a non-trivial label are retained, and clips with no flagged frames are discarded.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Motion-Compensated Perceptual Difference Mapping.</span>
Within each retained clip <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, consecutive frame pairs <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t,t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t,t+1)</annotation></semantics></math> are aligned using optical flow <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Flow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖥𝗅𝗈𝗐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Flow}</annotation></semantics></math> (Farnebäck or TV-L1), which warps the second frame <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> to the reference <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The spatial variant of the Learned Perceptual Image Patch Similarity metric <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{LPIPS}_{\text{spatial}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖫𝖯𝖨𝖯𝖲</mi><mtext>spatial</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{LPIPS}_{\text{spatial}}</annotation></semantics></math> is then applied to compute pixel-level perceptual activation maps <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, which are normalized to <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> to form interpretable heatmaps <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Clip-level severity is quantified by aggregating heatmap intensities via mean pooling, and the frame pair with the highest severity is selected as the representative artifact instance.
For interpretability, heatmaps are colorized and blended with the original frame (<math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>), and both raw heatmaps and overlays are saved to disk.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The pipeline returns, for each clip, the representative frame pair, associated severity score, and file paths to saved visualizations.
All results are summarized in structured JSON output, including clip boundaries, artifact categories, severity measures, and visualization paths.
This ensures reproducibility and facilitates integration with the broader VQA-Router framework for expert routing and perceptual quality assessment.</p>
</div>
